From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 128] panvk: decode BC6H once per block for the ASTC transcode
Generated-by: LLM

The BC6H transcoder ran the full per-mode BC6H decode for every texel of
every pass, and its unquantiser read a global is_signed that was never
set, so BC6H_SFLOAT blocks holding negative values decoded as large
positive ones (bright or infinite texels instead of 0).

Parse mode, endpoints, partition and the index stream once per block
(per-mode bit layouts generated from Mesa's bptc_float_modes table, with
the mode branches kept unflattened), then fetch each texel with a few
integer operations. Signedness comes from the format specialisation
constant. The decode matches Mesa's CPU BPTC decoder bit-exactly on
65536 random blocks for both UFLOAT and SFLOAT.

The HDR endpoint search now computes what the decoder will see for each
CEM 11 mode directly (the packed fields are lossless once clamped) and
bit-packs only the winner; weight/bit-count tables became arithmetic.
Output blocks are bit-identical to the per-texel version. No spills
(was 1153). biblioklept

Mali-G615 MC2, one 2048x2048 level: BC6H UFLOAT 137 -> 36 ms (random
blocks), 109 -> 34 ms (realistic blocks); SFLOAT 136 -> 37 ms,
110 -> 35 ms. PSNR unchanged on realistic data (54.33 / 49.84 dB);
SFLOAT random blocks 14.35 -> 24.09 dB from the sign fix.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/127

